Subject: [PATCH] minimum arm64: offer Installer on first boot

A fresh RENKU arm64 guest booted straight to the desktop from the live
medium, with no prompt to install -- the README's install steps (run
DriveSetup, then Installer, by hand from the Deskbar menu) are the only
way in, and nothing on screen says so.

Haiku already has the machinery for this: data/launch/user's `run`
job shows FirstBootPrompt (Desktop/Installer buttons) instead of the
plain desktop when `/system/bin/FirstBootPrompt` exists and the boot
volume is read-only (true for a live/install medium) or no locale has
been configured yet. FirstBootPrompt itself was just never added to
the minimum image -- the regular profile has always shipped it,
minimum never did, so that `file_exists` check failed and the `run`
job fell through to the plain desktop every time. Added to minimum's
SYSTEM_BIN the same way DriveSetup and Installer are already in
SYSTEM_APPS; no other change needed, the launch condition was already
there.

diff --git a/build/jam/images/definitions/minimum b/build/jam/images/definitions/minimum
index 01fc18c38e..58f18c6889 100644
--- a/build/jam/images/definitions/minimum
+++ b/build/jam/images/definitions/minimum
@@ -28,6 +28,7 @@ SYSTEM_BIN = [ FFilterByBuildFeatures
 	filepanel
 	finddir
 	findpaths
+	FirstBootPrompt
 	fortune
 	fstrim
 	ftpd
